# Limpet udev rules for the Bus Pirate 6 (BPIO2 interface), installed by
# limpet-plugin-buspirate-mcp.
#
# VID:PID 1209:7331 ("Bus Pirate Next Gen CDC", pid.codes-allocated) is taken from the
# BusPirate5-firmware repo, which also builds the BP6 (src/platform/bpi6-rev2.c/h live
# in the same tree as the BP5 platform files). usb_descriptors.c:32-37 documents two
# registered pid.codes pairs for this firmware family (1209:7331 CDC, 1209:7332 logic
# analyzer) and states "the firmware is hard-coded to use the first of these" — so BP6
# enumerates identically to the existing Bus Pirate v5 entry in
# limpet/hardware.d/03-multiprotocol-tools.toml. This is the authoritative firmware
# source that sets idVendor/idProduct, not a live lsusb capture (no BP6 unit was
# available to this worker to attach and read lsusb directly).
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="1209", ATTR{idProduct}=="7331", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess", TAG+="limpet-multiprotocol"
